[
  {
    "sha": "582d9dc80e9055387163119f17f1db040ff3bc4b",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVyT_AdoAKDU4MmQ5ZGM4MGU5MDU1Mzg3MTYzMTE5ZjE3ZjFkYjA0MGZmM2JjNGI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "sn3ro",
        "email": "zak.darek@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T05:39:26Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "sn3ro",
        "email": "zak.darek@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T05:39:26Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(drilling): Auto reads the depth in material; add the Deep cycle choice\n\nAuto chose the cycle by R plane - bottom, so the air above a hole's mouth\ncounted as depth: a 3.5 mm spot under a 5 mm gap posted G73 with an\n18 mm peck step. Auto now reads the depth from the mouth (or a lower R\nplane) in the axial cycle, the radial cycle (from d = 0, not the R\nstandoff) and the setup sheet, as the drill page note already did. The\nplunge still starts at the R plane.\n\nA new cycle choice Deep (\"deep\", \"Deep peck (full retract)\") posts the\nfull-retract peck (G83) on any hole. It is appended to the combo and the\ndigest, so older operations keep their indices and stamps. The cross-hole\ncycle maps it before its unreachable arm.\n\nFixes #2443\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
