  {
    "sha": "d5cd91ede645300fbe401aa0c443159b1cacc108",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVyT_AdoAKGQ1Y2Q5MWVkZTY0NTMwMGZiZTQwMWFhMGM0NDMxNTliMWNhY2MxMDg",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "sn3ro",
        "email": "zak.darek@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T12:40:35Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "sn3ro",
        "email": "zak.darek@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T12:40:35Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(drilling): Auto counts uncut stock over a mouth as depth\n\nThe quick gate showed that a depth from the mouth alone hides stock that\nstill stands over the hole (a raw bar r20 over a part r10). Auto now reads\nthe depth from the higher of the mouth and the material over it, clamped\nto the R plane:\n\n- axial holes: the app passes the material top over each drill disk\n  (part, raw stock, and the program ahead where the raw stock stands over\n  the mouth) as CycleParams::material_top;\n- radial holes: the raw stock's surface over the mouth, clamped to the\n  R standoff.\n\nThe setup sheet names the cycle the generator chose (the current cache),\nor \"auto\" without one.\n\nRefs #2443\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "cdbe84fed76805ece8c72f4715bf3afaaa49280e",
